Starting with 14. The positive factors of 14 are numbers that can multiply by another integer to get 14. Let's see: 1 × 14 = 14, 2 × 7 = 14. So the factors are 1, 2, 7, 14. Let me confirm that. Yeah, those are all the positive factors because 14 is not divisible by 3, 4, 5, etc. So factors of 14: {1, 2, 7, 14}.

